I've always played a Valkyrie for a few reasons. One, you can wear
virtually any armor without any combat penalties - meaning that by the
end, it takes a lot to bring you down. Two, you can get maximum
proficiency with daggers (and thus Magicbane), which greatly helps
when you're on your way to the bottom of Gehennom and don't feel like
taking the twenty-plus curses per turn that enemies are capable of
dishing out. Three, they gain HP like nothing. Four, the Valkyrie
quest is probably the easiest one out of all of them, and the reward
is one of the best artifacts in the game (nothing like having half
damage to go with that -60 AC and hundreds of HP).

My second choice would be a Monk. Sure, Master Kaen isn't exactly the
easiest quest of them all, but having resistance to everything (and
warning) early on is a very nice thing to have. Also, I THINK you get
a higher chance to hit with fists than any other class gets to hit
with their normal weapons (because you can go up to Grand Master in
unarmed combat).



